# Q55 (round 2): replace Q55* entries in /output/report.json (idempotent). Numbers from out/q55/{joint.log,joint_summary*.json,hyp_table.csv,norm_cont.csv,r10_core.csv}
import json
p='/output/report.json'; r=json.load(open(p))
r['results']=[x for x in r['results'] if not x['quantity'].startswith('Q55')]
A=lambda *s:[{'name':n,'value':v} for n,v in s]
def add(q,v,conf,tgt,unit,unc,ev,ass):
    r['results'].append({'quantity':q,'value':v,'confidence':conf,'target':tgt,'unit':unit,'uncertainty':unc,'evidence':ev,'assumptions':ass})

add('Q55a: HCN/HCO+ J-dependence of the N/S contrast at matched beams, 1-0 / 3-2 / 4-3 (revises the earlier "75% of the contrast is at J=1-0")',
"Tb (K km/s) ratios HCN/HCO+, fixed velocity windows, common circular beams. 1-0 from ONE cube (2016.1.00965 X94a spw27, both lines in one spw, 0.76x0.63\"): 1.0\" N 1.06+-0.06, S 0.73+-0.11 (N/S 1.45+-0.22); 2.5\" N 0.90+-0.02, S 0.62+-0.04 (N/S 1.44+-0.09); 2015.1.00993 (2.1x1.7\", complete flux) at 2.5\": N 0.906+-0.010, S 0.575+-0.013 (N/S 1.58+-0.04). 3-2 (Xb4d): 1.1\" N 0.835, S 0.402 (N/S 2.08); 2.5\" N 0.698, S 0.386 (N/S 1.81+-0.03). 4-3 (2018.1.00493 HCN + 2018.1.00223 HCO+): 1.0\" N 0.814+-0.019, S 0.222+-0.015 (N/S 3.7); 2.5\" N 0.624, S 0.174 (N/S 3.6); but the single-observation Xb47 4-3 at 4.5\" gives N 0.515, S 0.317 (N/S 1.6): the S HCN 4-3 flux of the high-resolution project is 0.61 of Xb47 (HCO+ 0.87, N HCN 0.88), so the 4-3 N/S contrast is uncertain between 1.6 and 3.7 (missing flux of extended HCN at S in the 0.9\" data vs N-S blending in the 4.5\" Xb47 beam). Consequence: ln(N/S) at 1-0 / 3-2 = 0.37/0.73 = 0.51 (core, 1.0-1.1\"), 0.61-0.77 (2.5\"): 50-75% of the 3-2 contrast (in log) is present at 1-0; the rest, and possibly more at 4-3, depends on J. 'Not mainly J-dependent excitation' is therefore weakened to 'about half or more of the contrast is J-independent'.",
'medium','N, S','ratio','0.04-0.2 in the ratios (stat + 5% model floor); 00965 loses 25-45% flux (72% N, 56% S of 00993 HCN) so its absolute 1-0 values are lower limits; 4-3 N/S unresolved 1.6-3.7',
'scripts/q55f_r10_core.py -> out/q55/r10_core.csv; out/q53/fixedwin_all.csv, fixedwin43.csv; out/q54/vs_hco.csv',
A(('beams','1.0, 2.5 arcsec circular (core); Tb ratios already in K km/s (q4_lib.kb); fixed window +-350 km/s'),('flux-loss','00965 HCN vs HCO+ recovery is common-mode only if both lines have the same extent')))

add('Q55b: matched-beam joint RADEX model comparison of the N/S contrast (Bayes factors; replaces the 3-datum chi2 of the first Q55b)',
"Model: one-zone RADEX slabs (LAMDA HCN, HCO+; H2; CMB; dv 150 km/s), per nucleus theta=(Tkin 20-150 K [5 values], log n 3-7.5, log N(HCN) 13-17.5, log X=N(HCN)/N(HCO+) -1..+1, 12C/13C 32/56/100), flat priors on the grid, N(HCN)/n<=10^12.5; likelihood: HCN/HCO+ Tb ratios R10, R32, R43 at ONE common beam + absolute integrated Tb of both lines in each J (beam filling <=1; this removes the optically thin/cold-S and hot-N 'T-only' solutions) + 13C/12C 1-0 (2015.1.00993, 2.2\") + H13CN 4-3 limit (alpha<0.10 N, <0.14 S); one calibration nuisance per J shared by N and S (7% / 5% / 25%), 5% model floor. 12 data sets; lnZ differences = ln Bayes factors (best = 0). [ln BF vs best] identical physics at N and S: -46 to -49 (R10,R32[,13C]); -61 to -131 with R43 and/or sub-arcsec absolute brightness: EXCLUDED in every data set (this is the only robust statement). Core 1.0-1.1\" (R10 00965, R32, R43, 13C, brightness) 'B_core3_13C': T-only -9.3, n-only -1.8, T+n (excitation) -1.7, X-only (abundance ratio, same HCN column) -8.2, N(HCN)-only -1.9, N(HCN)+X (column/opacity+abundance) -0.1, T+n+N(HCN) -0.9, all four free 0.0. Without R43 ('B_core3_no43_13C'): T -0.9, n -2.4, T+n -0.5, X -3.7, N(HCN) -1.1, N(HCN)+X 0.0, all free -0.1. 2.5\" set (R10,R32,13C, 'A_no43'): X-only 0.0, N(HCN)+X 0.0, T -3.4, n -5.5, T+n -4.0, N(HCN) -4.7, all free -1.6. With R43 (00493/00223) 'A_full': N(HCN)+X 0.0, all free -1.4, N(HCN) -4.1, T -8.2, n -7.8, X-only -14.5; with the Xb47 R43 'A_43Xb47': X-only 0.0, N(HCN)+X -1.1, n -6.2, T -9.7. Posterior probability with flat prior over the 8 non-null hypotheses (computed, hypotheses overlap): B_core3_13C: all-free 0.36, N(HCN)+X 0.32, T+n+N 0.14, T+n 0.07, n 0.06, N(HCN) 0.05, X <0.01, T <0.01; A_no43: X 0.44, N(HCN)+X 0.44, rest <0.1. RESULT: (i) identical physics is excluded; (ii) a T-only difference is disfavoured when absolute brightness and R43 are used (lnBF -3 to -14), allowed (-0.9) at the core without R43; (iii) n-only and N(HCN)-only are disfavoured (-2 to -8) once 13C is used; (iv) an HCN/HCO+ column-ratio (abundance) difference alone is disfavoured at 1\" with 13C (-4 to -8) but allowed at 2.5\" and with the Xb47 R43; (v) a joint column+abundance difference (best-fit N: N(HCN)=10^16.25-16.75, tau32(HCN) 4-10, S: 10^14.5-15, tau32 0.1-0.5, log n 6.75, logX_N ~0, logX_S ~-0.25) is best or within 1.1 of best in all 12 data sets, but excitation (T+n) differences are within 1.7 at the core. THE DATA DO NOT DISCRIMINATE between a column/opacity-plus-abundance difference and an excitation (T,n) difference; 3 data per nucleus (R10,R32,R43) for 4-5 parameters cannot. Sensitivity: all column/opacity solutions sit at 12C/13C=100 (prior edge, P=0.87-1.0); capping 12C/13C<=56 costs ~3-4 in lnZ and reshuffles the core ranking (B_core3_13C: all free 0.0, T+n+N 0.1, T+n 1.0, T 7.6, n 4.5, X 12.9, N(HCN)+X 5.3), i.e. the opacity preference is conditional on a high 12C/13C.",
'low','N, S','ln Bayes factor','grid steps (0.25 dex in N, X, n; 5 temperatures; 3 isotope ratios); hypothesis ranking changes with the 4-3 input (00493/00223 vs Xb47) and with the 12C/13C prior',
'scripts/q55d_radex13.py (low-column RADEX), q55e_joint.py (model comparison; X13MAX=1.75 TAG=_X13le56 for the cap), q55h_tables.py -> out/q55/joint.log, joint_summary.json, joint_X13le56.log, hyp_table.csv/.md',
A(('inputs','2.5" set: R10 00993, R32 Xb4d, R43 00493/00223 (fixed windows, Q53), 13C Q47 (H13CN/HCN N 0.021+-0.007, S 0.0065+-0.008; H13CO+/HCO+ N 0.023+-0.007, S 0.013+-0.007, flux ratios x1.054 to Tb); core set: R10 1.06/0.73 (00965), R32 0.835/0.402 (1.1"), R43 0.814/0.222 (1.0")'),
  ('caveats','the 13C data are 2.2" ratios applied to a 1" core; single zone, same T and n for HCN and HCO+; grid edges (T 20/150 K, 12C/13C 100) are reached by several posteriors; the old 6-datum test (q55_ns_single_param.py, out/q55/ns_single_param.log) mixed 2-6" beams and is superseded and not used')))

add('Q55c: absolute normalisation of the contrast: HCN, HNC, CN, HCO+ per unit 1.3 mm continuum (matched beams), which species deviates',
"Line integral (K km/s, same windows as the ratios) divided by the Xb4d 1.3 mm continuum (mJy per circular beam, same beam), then N/S. Continuum N/S = 1.08 (1.1\"), 1.0 (1.0\"), 1.26 (1.4\"), 1.44 (1.9\"), 1.54 (2.5\"); i.e. at 1\" N and S have equal 1.3 mm continuum (5.2 vs 4.8 mJy/beam). N/S of line/continuum: 3-2 at 1.1\": HCN 3.1, HNC 3.0, CN 3.2, HCO+ 1.44; at 2.5\": HCN 1.85, HNC 1.97, CN 2.8, HCO+ 1.02. 4-3 at 1.0\": HCN 4.0, HCO+ 1.25. 1-0 (00965, 1.0\"): HCN 3.9, HCO+ 2.7; 2.5\": HCN 1.9, HCO+ 1.3. Reading: per unit dust, HCN, HNC and CN are ~3x stronger at N at 1\" (a coherent family), HCO+ only ~1.3-1.4x at 3-2/4-3 (2.7x at 1-0, J-dependent). So the species that deviates at S relative to N is the HCN/HNC/CN family (deficit at S, or enhancement/thickness at N), not an HCO+ excess; the previously leading 'HCO+ excess at S' hypothesis is NOT supported and is withdrawn. Caveats that this is not an abundance ratio: (a) N(H2) ∝ S_cont/Td, so every line/H2 N/S ratio is multiplied by Td_N/Td_S (unknown; 0.5-2 gives HCN 1.5-6.2, HCO+ 0.7-2.9): HCN-family N>S holds for Td_N/Td_S>=0.5, HCO+ can be flat for Td_N/Td_S~0.7; (b) the 1.3 mm continuum is optically thin (peak Tb ~0.08 K at 1.1\") but S may contain non-dust (synchrotron/free-free), which would lower the line/dust ratio at N relative to S by up to the non-dust fraction; (c) the lines are thick at N (Q55b), so line/dust is not N(X)/N(H2). CO/C18O in matched beams was not available in the cached cubes.",
'medium','N, S','N/S ratio of line/continuum','~10% (line errors + beam-matched continuum sampling), plus the unquantified Td_N/Td_S (0.5-2) and S non-dust fraction',
'scripts/q55g_norm.py -> out/q55/norm_cont.csv',
A(('continuum','Xb4d spw25_27_29_31 pbcor continuum convolved to the common circular beam with the exact beam-difference kernel, sampled at the N and S positions'),('lines','HCN/HCO+ 3-2 Xb4d, HNC/CN 3-2 (00412, 00493), 4-3 (00493/00223), 1-0 (00965); 00965 loses 25-45% flux')))

add('Q55d: temperature: reconciliation of Q55b with Q42/Q49 and forum p0054-r01, p0057 (probability of the sign of Tc_N - Tc_S)',
"Matched-beam joint test (Q55b): T-only difference lnBF -0.9 to -14 depending on data set; P(Tkin_N>Tkin_S) in the all-parameters-free model (independent N and S marginals, calibration nuisance ignored) = 0.76 (A_full), 0.39 (A_no43), 0.13 (A_43Xb47), 0.44 (B_core3_13C), 0.27 (B_core3_no43_13C), 0.30 (B_core3_no43), i.e. 0.13-0.76, no sign preferred. The first Q55b (R10 Michiyama, R21 Xb55, R32 Xb4f in different beams) found a T-only solution with N colder (median -30 K): it mixed beams, had 3 data per nucleus and no absolute brightness, and is withdrawn. Q42/Q49: Tc_N unconstrained (profile dchi2<5 over 10-150 K), Tc_S=17+-1 K, P(Tc_N<=30 K)=0.33+-0.12 (base) / 0.64+-0.09 (no 1-0); p0054-r01 (team-b) prefers a hot N core; the two-zone SMC/nested fits depend on the envelope prior (P(Te>=50 K)=0.11-0.7). All three are the same statement: temperature is undecided and prior dependent (P(Tc_N>Tc_S) between ~0.15 and ~0.75, i.e. no sign preferred). IR pumping (p0057, team-b: no HCN-vib in N, N like vib-non-detected galaxies; ours: v2=1f Tb/Tb(v=0) 3-2 N<0.059/S<0.080 at 0.24\", N<0.030/S<0.048 at 0.95\", N<0.024/S<0.049 at 6\", Tvib<290-380 K N, 350-430 K S): excludes strong pumping, not NGC 4418-like Tvib 200-300 K. Q51/Q52 are not used.",
'low','N, S','probability / K','sign probability 0.13-0.76 across data sets (binary sign, not a calibrated posterior)',
'out/q55/joint_summary.json (P(T_N>T_S)); Q42/Q49/Q50 entries; forum p0054-r01, p0057',
A(('independence','P(sign) computed from the N and S marginals under the all-free model, not from the joint (the shared calibration nuisance is ignored)')))

add('Q55e: discriminating predictions of the surviving interpretations and the observation needed',
"Posterior-predictive opacity factor f=(H13CN/HCN Tb ratio)x(12C/13C) (f=1.05 optically thin, f>>1 thick 12C), core data set B_core3_13C [N / S, median]: column+abundance (N(HCN),X differ) H13CN/HCN 1-0 f=2.7 [2.7-3.4] / 1.08, H13CO+/HCO+ 2.05 / 1.08, H13CN/HCN 4-3 2.2 [2.2-4.2] / 1.06, tau32(HCN) 6.8 [6.8-10.6] / 0.18; all free 2.2 [1.4-2.6] / 1.15, 4-3 2.9 / 1.08, tau32 5.2 / 0.54; excitation (T,n differ) 1.10 / 1.60, tau32 0.23 / 2.4; n-only 1.7 / 2.9 (N thinner than S); T-only 1.07 / 1.22; abundance-only X 2.6 / 2.6. The N/S ratio of H13CN/HCN (1-0) is the discriminant: 2.5 (column+abundance), 1.9 (all free), 1.0 (abundance only), 0.9 (T only), 0.7 (T,n), 0.6 (n only); the same for H13CO+/HCO+ 1-0 (1.9, 1.4, 0.7, 1.0, 0.8, 0.8). With 12C/13C=100 the predicted H13CN/HCN 1-0 is N 0.027, S 0.011 (column+abundance) against measured N 0.021+-0.007, S 0.0065+-0.008 at 2.2\" (2015.1.00993; Q47): current N/S = 3+-3.5 (1 sigma), no discrimination. Required: sigma(H13CN/HCN)~0.003 at S (3-4 sigma between 0.011 and 0.027 at N), i.e. ~(0.008/0.003)^2 = 7x the 2015.1.00993 integration at its 2.2\" beam (the same at 1\" would cost ~90x because the S brightness is beam diluted: 1\" is not feasible, tapered 2\" is); H13CO+ 1-0 in the same spw gives an independent check (predicted N/S 1.9 vs 0.7-1.0). The H13CN 4-3 limit (alpha<0.10 N), now in the likelihood, already removes the thickest N solutions (f43>~5); the 2018.1.00223 X858 spw29 cube (341.78-343.65 GHz, 0.3-1\" beam) covers H13CN 4-3 but the CO 3-2 line sits 385 km/s away (attempt with a polynomial baseline fails: not usable without the wing models of Q47a), and no cached cube covers H13CO+ 3-2/4-3 or H13CN 3-2. H13CN/H13CO+ 1-0 are in 2015.1.00993 (used, 2.2\") and 2016.1.00965 spw25 (0.77\", loses 25-45% flux, H13CO+ blended with SiO 2-1 at +315 km/s, H13CN at the band edge: not measured). A thermometer at the N core (CH3CN/HC3N/CH3OH at 1\") remains needed for T.",
'low','N, S','ratio','predictions are model (grid) medians; N/S measured 3+-3.5; 12C/13C (32-100) is a nuisance',
'out/q55/joint_summary.json (fH10, fO10, fH43 quantiles); out/q47/ratios10.json; Q47a',
A(('X13','the opacity factor removes the 12C/13C dependence except through the posterior (columns sit at 12C/13C=100)'),('S/N','scaling from the 2015.1.00993 ratio errors (0.006-0.009), no new sensitivity calculation')))

TABLE=("TEST TABLE (what each test excludes; surviving Q47/Q49/Q50/Q42/Q4/Q54/Q53 values; Q51/Q52 not used) | "
"(1) HCN v2=1f (IR pumping, Q4; p0057 agrees): 3sigma Tb(v2=1f)/Tb(v=0) 3-2 N<0.059/S<0.080 (0.24\"), N<0.030/S<0.048 (0.95\"), N<0.024/S<0.049 (6\"); 4-3 N<0.028/S<0.087: Tvib<290-380 K (N), 350-430 K (S). EXCLUDES strong pumping at both nuclei; does not exclude NGC 4418-like 200-300 K (alpha<0.03) or a <47 pc buried source diluted in the beam. | "
"(2) H13CN 4-3 (Q47a): alpha<0.10 (N), <0.14 (S), 3sigma; RADEX predicts alpha 0.02-0.03 at n<=3e5 and 0.05-0.12 at n>=1e6: informative only at n>=1e6 (removes 50-65% of the N posterior in Q50, the thickest N solutions f43>~5 here); leaves Tc_N 13-110 K. Opacity not excluded. | "
"(3) 13C 1-0 at 2.2\" (Q47b): H13CN/HCN N 0.021+-0.007, S 0.0065+-0.008; H13CO+/HCO+ N 0.023+-0.007, S 0.013+-0.007; X_S/X_N median 0.98 (0.65-1.58), the posterior fills its prior: neither abundance nor opacity difference detected or excluded; N/S of H13CN/HCN = 3+-3.5. In Q55b the columns/opacity solutions need 12C/13C~100. | "
"(4) J-dependence at matched beams (Q55a): HCN/HCO+ N/S 1.45+-0.22 (1-0, 1.0\"), 2.08 (3-2, 1.1\"), 3.7 (4-3, 1.0\", uncertain 1.6-3.7); ln ratio 1-0 / 3-2 = 0.5-0.75: about half or more of the contrast is J-independent. EXCLUDES a contrast produced by J-dependent excitation alone; not a pure column effect either. | "
"(5) Joint matched-beam RADEX model comparison (Q55b): identical physics EXCLUDED (lnBF<=-46); T-only, n-only, N(HCN)-only and abundance-only differences each disfavoured by lnBF 2-14 in most data sets; column+abundance and all-free best or within 1; T+n within 1.7 at the core: NOT decided (3 data per nucleus). | "
"(6) Tc_N (Q42/Q49/Q50/Q55d): unconstrained 12-95 K; Tc_S=17+-1 K; sign of Tc_N-Tc_S undecided (P(T_N>T_S) 0.13-0.76); p0054-r01 hot N and Q55b-old colder N are both prior/data-set dependent. | "
"(7) Chemistry and normalisation (Q54, Q55c): CN/HCN and HNC/HCN lower at S, HCN/HNC/CN fall together vs HCO+ (N/S per dust 3.0-3.2 at 1\" vs HCO+ 1.4): no XDR/AGN signature; the deviating species is the HCN/HNC/CN family relative to dust (Td_N/Td_S and optical depth uncertain), HCO+ excess at S not supported. CH3OH/H2 S/N 1.9-7.7 (N CH3OH 1.8sigma): shock/outflow at S, extended, absent at 0.95\".")
add('Q55f: synthesis table of tests of the cause of the N/S HCN/HCO+ contrast (N 1.0 vs S 0.44 at 50-120 pc, factor 2.1+-0.2), revised',TABLE,'medium','N, S','ratios / K / ln BF / probability',
'see rows; robust: strong IR pumping excluded, identical physics at N and S excluded, not an HCN-specific XDR chemistry, not J-dependent excitation alone',
'Q55a-e; report entries Q4/Q4c (v2=1f), Q47a-c, Q42/Q49/Q50, Q54, Q53; forum p0050-r01, p0053, p0054, p0054-r01, p0055, p0056, p0057',
A(('scope','mutually non-exclusive causes; no subjective weights are given (the previous 0.45/0.30/0.15 weights and the "HCO+ excess at S" lead are withdrawn)')))

add('Q55g: verdict, unresolved part, diagnostic implication',
"VERDICT (derived from Q55a-f, no subjective weights): EXCLUDED: (i) strong IR pumping (Tvib>~300-430 K); (ii) identical excitation/column at N and S (Bayes factor e^-46 or lower in every matched-beam data set); (iii) an HCN-specific XDR/AGN chemistry (CN/HCN and HNC/HCN lower at S, the HCN/HNC/CN family falls together); (iv) a contrast produced by J-dependent excitation alone (50-75% of it in log is already present at J=1-0). DISFAVOURED (model/data-set dependent, lnBF 2-14): a pure T difference, a pure n difference, a pure N(HCN) difference, and (at 1\" with 13C) a pure abundance-ratio difference. NOT DECIDED: column/opacity-plus-abundance (N optically thick tau32(HCN)~4-10, S thin-to-moderate) versus excitation (T,n) differences at the N core: lnBF within 1.7 at 1\"; the result flips with the 4-3 input (00493/00223 vs Xb47) and with 12C/13C (100 vs <=56). The 'HCO+ excess at S' is not supported: per unit dust the HCN/HNC/CN family is ~3x brighter at N and HCO+ only ~1.4x. DIAGNOSTIC IMPLICATION (with Q53): the S (AGN) value 0.44 is the lower of the two nuclei and is below published starburst values at J=1-0,3-2,4-3; the N core 1.0 is starburst-like at >=188 pc; since the contrast is not an AGN-specific chemistry and is at least half J-independent, HCN/HCO+ at 50-100 pc reflects column/opacity or excitation structure of the thick HCN lines, and an AGN-dominated nucleus here has a LOW ratio, i.e. HCN/HCO+ >1 is not required of an AGN. DECISIVE OBSERVATION: H13CN/HCN and H13CO+/HCO+ 1-0 at N and S in a tapered ~2\" beam at sigma~0.003 (about 7x the 2015.1.00993 integration), predicted N/S ratio 2.5 (column/opacity) vs 0.6-1.0 (excitation, n, T or abundance only); a matched-uv 4-3 HCN/HCO+ (single observation, both lines in one tuning, 1\") to settle the 4-3 N/S contrast 1.6 vs 3.7; a 1\" thermometer (CH3CN/HC3N/CH3OH) at the N core.",
'low','N, S','text','see Q55b, Q55e: the discriminating power is limited by 3 data per nucleus, the 4-3 input and the 12C/13C prior',
'Q55a-f; Q53 (diagnostic); Q54 (chemistry)',
A(('literature','Harada+2018 (1.7" HCN/HCO+ 1-0, 3-2, Table 13), Michiyama+2018 (1-0 2.1x1.7"), Izumi+2016 and Imanishi+2019 (compilations used in Q53), Sakamoto+2010/Aalto+2015 (Tvib), Jimenez-Donaire+2017 (H13CN/H13CO+ opacity of dense-gas tracers in nearby disks), Nakajima+2023 (NGC 1068 abundances): context only, not used quantitatively here'),('limits','one-zone RADEX; 3 data per nucleus; 12C/13C 32-100 prior')))
r['interpretation']=('Q55 (synthesis, round 2): the N/S HCN/HCO+ contrast is not IR pumping, not an HCN-specific AGN chemistry, not J-dependent excitation alone and not identical physics; matched-beam joint RADEX Bayes factors disfavour single-parameter T, n and N(HCN) differences, and abundance-only at 1 arcsec with 13C, but cannot separate a column/opacity-plus-abundance difference (N thick, S thinner) from a (T,n) excitation difference; per unit dust the HCN/HNC/CN family is ~3x brighter at N, HCO+ ~1.4x. See Q55a-g. '+r['interpretation'].split('See Q55a-c. ',1)[-1])
json.dump(r,open(p,'w'),indent=1)
